WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:05.100
This is again an eye tracking study. The
darker colors... so the closer you get to

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:10.410
red is where there's more attention on
the region of interest. So what you'll

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:16.710
notice here is there's various attention.
What's really curious to me about

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:20.550
this picture is... my adviser Phil
Zimbardo always taught me to be my

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:22.138
own first subject always.

00:00:22.138 --> 00:00:24.869
So I always run myself as my first subject.

00:00:24.869 --> 00:00:28.740
And I always end up being an outlier
and completely not instructive for other people.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:32.240
So when I looked at this study the thing I
fixated on was the gun.

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:35.360
And you know like nobody's paying attention to the gun.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:41.910
It's really sort of interesting. But you'll see differential attention so

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:43.808
What the Conservatives are paying
attention to are

00:00:43.808 --> 00:00:45.539
the emblems of authority.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:47.720
The patch is about: "I'm a cop," right?

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:50.039
Like, I'm the Law &amp; Order.

00:00:50.039 --> 00:00:52.392
Whereas what liberals are paying attention to

00:00:52.392 --> 00:00:54.569
is the person getting the beat down.

00:00:54.569 --> 00:00:58.680
And to a certain degree, liberals are also paying attention--

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:03.000
(I didn't Circle it) but, to the cane.
This is a disabled person.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.860
Not a single conservative paid any
attention at all to the cane.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:08.440
So there's real differences in what people

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:10.480
are paying attention to. It's not, again,

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:13.740
just an issue of interpretation.
It's an issue of perception.

00:01:13.747 --> 00:01:17.880
Why is this important?
This is important because it can predict

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:20.640
important political choices that people make.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:22.340
About policy issues.

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:25.580
So in the image that I just showed you, which is

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:30.960
this same image, you can actually look at how
liberals and conservatives respond differently.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:34.140
And then the other thing we
manipulated was the story we told.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:35.585
There was a 30-second narrative.

00:01:35.585 --> 00:01:38.220
So in some of the narratives we called it a beat down.

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:41.759
And in some of the other narratives we
called it an arrest. And you'll notice

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:44.020
conservatives don't change at all

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:47.440
how they look at the image based on the narration.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:53.660
But liberals completely change the way 
that they think about it

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:57.160
when you call it a beat down versus an arrest.

00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:00.260
Why is this important? Because different people

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:01.960
respond to different stimuli differently.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:04.520
So in other words some people are much more visual

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:07.000
and some people are much more auditory.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:10.040
Here you see in this particular instance that

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:14.800
the reactivity on that, the auditory reactivity, is liberal.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:17.440
In this which is a different image of a woman

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:22.560
looking at a coffin. Where we said he died in combat,

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:25.080
versus he was a looter. You'll see that the difference

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:28.628
in perception changes as a function
of somebody being conservative.

00:02:28.628 --> 00:02:30.980
Again these are things that you can run

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:33.260
not just with liberals and conservatives, but with other

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:36.700
categorizations as well.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:40.640
When we run these with men versus women,

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:42.300
they're always really funny because

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:44.120
the men never pay attention to the narration.

00:02:44.129 --> 00:02:47.280
It's all about the, it's all about the image.

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:52.420
But in these it's reactive based on whether or not

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:54.500
people are liberal or conservative

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:57.020
and how they look at the image.

00:02:57.020 --> 00:03:01.080
Similarly in the sex differences one we had an image

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:04.106
you saw the one with Madonna and Britney Spears.

00:03:04.106 --> 00:03:07.463
You can see the amount of time they
spend looking at the necklace.

00:03:07.463 --> 00:03:10.514
In the other one, it's a picture of a soldier

00:03:10.514 --> 00:03:14.310
holding an injured child. And you can look at differences

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:18.209
(here I want to show you how you can
divide it up by sex differences)

00:03:18.209 --> 00:03:21.090
There's differences in men and women
looking at the child's face

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:22.000
versus the child's body.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.640
So these aren't just ideological things.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:26.160
You can also look at sex differences as well.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:28.560
Although we've been primarily interested in the

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.544
ideological differences.

00:03:30.544 --> 00:03:34.420
Again these help you predict policy preferences:

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:36.900
so we have people look at certain images

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:39.280
and then find out [ask people]

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:41.680
"Did we make a mistake sending troops into Iraq?"

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:44.100
Or "Do you think--" this was done a little while ago

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:47.720
"Do you think the US can or will win the war in Iraq?"

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:50.139
And you can predict people's response

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:52.020
to that policy question based on

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:54.000
how much time they spend looking at particular

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.720
parts of the image. So if they're spending a lot of

00:03:56.730 --> 00:04:01.260
attention looking at the flag you can
see that that predicts their answer to

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:08.310
whether or not they think that the US
made a mistake in entering the war in

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:12.359
Iraq and so on and we've done numerous
ones of these about forty of them and

00:04:12.359 --> 00:04:19.380
their end up being pretty consistent so
there are particular categories of

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:25.050
things that people care about and you
can look at this again by liberal or

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:29.430
conservative here I'm just listing
some of the Apes some of the Preferences

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:33.210
of people that are particularly
concerned with protection which on

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:36.509
average tend to be people on the right
of the political spectrum

00:04:36.509 --> 00:04:41.009
none of these constellations should
surprise people who for example have

00:04:41.009 --> 00:04:45.000
been watching the Republican National
Convention so what does this have to do

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:51.150
with genes there was a report a while
ago liberals you know research is

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:55.889
finding the liberal gene that is beyond
ridiculous right why is it ridiculous

00:04:55.889 --> 00:04:59.729
it's ridiculous for several important
reasons first most importantly there is

00:04:59.729 --> 00:05:04.740
no such thing right why is there no such
thing why can there never be any such

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:09.000
thing because genes aren't that simple
there are multiple genes there are

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:12.030
multiple pathways these things are
multifactorial

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:16.590
they work in complicated interaction
with environmental factors so you're

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:20.820
never gonna find one single thing that's
gonna help you understand the liberal

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:24.690
gene or the conservative gene these
things are very complex and it's not

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:29.039
just Physiology it's not just genetics
but it's also not just environment they

00:05:29.039 --> 00:05:34.169
work together what does that mean it
means that DNA isn't your destiny genes

00:05:34.169 --> 00:05:38.610
contribute to these political outcomes
but they're not the only thing that

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:49.980
matters the environmental factors also
matter quite a bit

00:05:51.670 --> 00:05:53.730
you

